  "term": "spatial relationships",
  "definition": "In research methods, spatial relationships refers to how variables are connected across geographic or physical locations. The packet supports this idea through spatial regression methods, which examine these location-based patterns by accounting for spatial dependency, spatial autocorrelation, and regional variation.",
